{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"mig57-group-1","type":"group","x":0,"y":240,"width":1640,"height":860,"label":"1 · Lewis：原部门损失、私人收入与资本吸收","color":"6"},
		{"id":"mig57-group-2","type":"group","x":0,"y":1180,"width":1640,"height":820,"label":"2 · Fei–Ranis：劳动移出之后，食品怎样供养工业","color":"4"},
		{"id":"mig57-group-3","type":"group","x":0,"y":2080,"width":1640,"height":800,"label":"3 · Harris–Todaro：概率、迁移选择与双原点图","color":"5"},
		{"id":"mig57-group-4","type":"group","x":0,"y":2920,"width":1640,"height":600,"label":"4 · 比较政策：改变工资与增加岗位是不同实验","color":"2"},
		{"id":"mig57-group-5","type":"group","x":0,"y":3600,"width":1640,"height":640,"label":"5 · 回到统计：先判就业状态，再分别算人数与率","color":"3"},
		{"id":"mig57-group-6","type":"group","x":0,"y":4320,"width":1640,"height":600,"label":"6 · 扩展：家庭风险分担机制与循环迁移形态","color":"6"},
		{"id":"mig57-intro","type":"text","x":0,"y":0,"width":1640,"height":180,"text":"# 二元经济与劳动力迁移\n\n连续阅读：[[02_Economy/10_发展经济学/10_二元经济与劳动力迁移|课程10]]。按编号向下，各区内顺着短边比较；点击卡片标题打开共享原子。颜色只区分问题，不表示核验或掌握状态。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nRead the numbered sections from top to bottom. Follow local connections and open card titles for the shared atoms. Colour distinguishes questions, not verification or mastery.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"mig57-001","type":"text","x":40,"y":300,"width":400,"height":300,"color":"6","text":"## [[Lewis 二元经济模型]]\n\n按资本使用与生产组织划分两部门；资本积累吸收劳动，不是把城乡直接分成两类。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nSectors differ by capital use and production organization. Accumulation absorbs labour; the division is not simply rural versus urban.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"mig57-002","type":"text","x":620,"y":300,"width":400,"height":300,"color":"6","text":"## [[剩余劳动力]]\n\n在明确调整条件下可移出而不显著减产的劳动；有限移出量须检查整个区间。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nLabour can leave with little output loss under specified adjustments. A finite withdrawal requires checking the whole interval.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"mig57-003","type":"text","x":1200,"y":300,"width":400,"height":300,"color":"6","text":"## [[边际产出与退出收入|无损退出 ≠ 零私人收入]]\n\n原产出不减，退出者仍可能放弃消费份额；生产边际与私人选择条件分别判断。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nOutput can remain unchanged while a departing worker gives up consumption. Production loss and private income forgone are different margins.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"mig57-004","type":"text","x":40,"y":700,"width":400,"height":300,"color":"6","text":"## [[无限劳动供给]]\n\n一定阶段内能按近乎不变工资增雇劳动；收入基准、溢价、招工及计价条件须稳定。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nAdditional workers are available at a near-constant wage over a phase, with stable outside income, recruitment and valuation conditions.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"mig57-005","type":"text","x":620,"y":700,"width":400,"height":300,"color":"6","text":"## [[利润再投与劳动吸收|再投何时扩大雇佣]]\n\n实际生产投资提高劳动需求，且工资与招工条件不变时，重新求得更高雇佣。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nProductive reinvestment expands employment when it raises labour demand while wages and recruitment conditions remain unchanged.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"mig57-income-bridge","type":"text","x":1200,"y":700,"width":400,"height":320,"text":"### 跨区桥：先固定分配规则\n\n[[边际产出与退出收入|家庭例]]随留守人数重新均分；[[农业短缺点与商业化点|Fei阶段I–II]]固定初始制度收入 $b$。两种规则不能在推导中切换。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nThe household example recalculates equal shares; Fei Phases I–II retain initial institutional income. Do not switch rules within a derivation.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"mig57-010","type":"text","x":40,"y":1240,"width":400,"height":300,"color":"4","text":"## [[费景汉–拉尼斯模型]]\n\n农业释放劳动与食品，工业积累资本并吸收劳动；持续转移还受消费分配和价格约束。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nAgriculture supplies labour and food; industry accumulates capital and hires. Consumption arrangements and relative prices constrain continued transfer.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"mig57-011","type":"text","x":620,"y":1240,"width":400,"height":300,"color":"4","text":"## [[农业短缺点与商业化点|短缺点 ≠ 商业化点]]\n\n基准短缺点关注每名工业劳动者的食品供养；商业化点是农业边际产出达到制度收入。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nThe baseline shortage point concerns food per industrial worker; commercialization occurs when agricultural marginal product reaches institutional income.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"mig57-014","type":"text","x":1200,"y":1240,"width":400,"height":300,"color":"4","text":"## [[食品价格与工业工资|食品变贵何时推高工业工资]]\n\n固定食品收入与工资挂钩比例时，食品相对工业品变贵会抬高工业品计价工资。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nWith food income and the wage linkage fixed, dearer food relative to industrial goods raises the industrial-goods wage.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"mig57-012","type":"text","x":40,"y":1640,"width":400,"height":300,"color":"4","text":"## [[农业剩余]]\n\n农业产出减留农者消费，得到可供非农人口的产品；不是剩余劳动或企业利润。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nAgricultural output less rural consumption leaves goods for non-agricultural people, not surplus labour or business profit.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"mig57-013","type":"text","x":620,"y":1640,"width":400,"height":300,"color":"4","text":"## [[平均农业剩余]]\n\n农业剩余除以正的工业劳动人数；总剩余增加，也可能赶不上供养人数增长。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nDivide agricultural surplus by positive industrial employment. Total surplus can rise while food available per industrial worker falls.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"mig57-food-bridge","type":"text","x":1200,"y":1640,"width":400,"height":320,"text":"### 价格反馈须另给条件\n\nAAS下降不能唯一决定食品价格。课堂工资水平线延至商业化点，还须固定相对价格及工资比例。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nFalling AAS does not uniquely determine food prices. A wage line flat until commercialization additionally requires fixed relative prices and wage proportions.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"mig57-020","type":"text","x":40,"y":2140,"width":400,"height":300,"color":"5","text":"## [[Harris–Todaro模型]]\n\n比较城市预期收入与农村收入；迁移改变竞争池，因此可在仍有城市失业时停止。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nMigration responds to expected urban versus rural earnings and changes the competing pool. Equilibrium may retain urban unemployment.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"mig57-022","type":"text","x":620,"y":2140,"width":400,"height":300,"color":"5","text":"## [[城市就业概率换算|岗位比例何时是个人概率]]\n\n先定义竞争者、分配规则与时期；同质周期随机分配下，每人的概率为 $M/S$。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nDefine competitors, allocation and timing. Homogeneous periodic random assignment supports the same probability $M/S$ for each worker.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"mig57-021","type":"text","x":1200,"y":2140,"width":400,"height":300,"color":"5","text":"## [[迁移收益现值|统一收益期限、成本与风险]]\n\n比较同一期限的迁移与留乡收入；一次性费用、持续费用和风险评价不能混算。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nCompare moving and staying over one horizon. Separate one-off and recurring costs, and state how income risk is valued.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"mig57-023","type":"text","x":40,"y":2540,"width":400,"height":300,"color":"5","text":"## [[迁移双原点图|从相反原点读取劳动配置]]\n\n先分清农业劳动、城市竞争池与岗位量；预期收入交点不是两部门实际工资相等。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nSeparate rural labour, the urban pool and jobs. The equilibrium crossing equates expected earnings, not realised sectoral wages.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"mig57-probability-bridge","type":"text","x":620,"y":2540,"width":980,"height":240,"text":"### 概率事件与图线要对应\n\n周期岗位分配的 $M/S$ 与“新空缺 ÷ 尚未获聘者”对应不同事件。双原点图的 $qq'$ 是预期收入轨迹，不是企业劳动需求；用于现值的概率还须与实际工作时长一致。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nPeriodic job allocation differs from conditional hiring into new vacancies. The diagram's expected-income locus is not labour demand. Present values also require probabilities that match paid working time.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"mig57-024","type":"text","x":260,"y":2980,"width":400,"height":300,"color":"2","text":"## [[城市工资与迁移反应|加工资未必增失业人数]]\n\n工资改变获聘后的报酬和企业成本；岗位需求、迁移及农村收入要一起调整。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nWages change pay conditional on employment and firms' costs. Jobs, migration and rural earnings must adjust together.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"mig57-025","type":"text","x":980,"y":2980,"width":400,"height":300,"color":"2","text":"## [[岗位创造与诱致迁移|新增岗位何时增失业人数]]\n\n在无其他城市就业的基准中，新增城市劳动力超过新增岗位才增加失业人数；率未必上升。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nWith no other urban jobs, unemployment counts rise if induced workers outnumber new jobs. The unemployment rate need not rise.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"mig57-shock-bridge","type":"text","x":40,"y":3320,"width":1560,"height":180,"text":"### 两种冲击，分别重求均衡\n\n提高工资不能同时把企业岗位需求默认为固定；外生增岗也不能把迁移人数任意指定。先说明哪些条件不变，再解竞争池与农村收入。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nA wage change need not leave jobs fixed, and job creation does not permit arbitrary induced migration. State what is held constant, then solve the urban pool and rural earnings.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"mig57-informal","type":"text","x":260,"y":3660,"width":400,"height":300,"color":"3","text":"## [[非正规就业]]\n\n有酬或营利工作未获相关正式安排覆盖；仍然是就业，不能自动设零收入或算失业。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nWork for pay or profit lacks relevant formal coverage. It remains employment, not automatically zero earnings or unemployment.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"mig57-unemployment","type":"text","x":980,"y":3660,"width":400,"height":300,"color":"3","text":"## [[失业率]]\n\n失业人数除以就业与失业人数之和；须按调查核对未就业、求职与可工作条件。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nUnemployment divided by the labour force requires the survey's joblessness, search and availability criteria, not total population as denominator.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"mig57-count-rate-bridge","type":"text","x":40,"y":3980,"width":1560,"height":200,"text":"### 未获现代岗位、失业人数 $U$、失业率 $u$ 是三次判断\n\n只有未获岗位者都符合失业口径时，才能写 $U=S-M$、$u=U/S$。城市劳动力80→92、岗位40→50时，$U$为40→42，$u$却为50%→45.65%；该配置比较本身不是政策因果证据。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nPeople without modern jobs must first satisfy unemployment criteria. In the constructed allocation, the count rises from 40 to 42 while the rate falls from 50% to 45.65%. This accounting comparison does not identify a policy effect.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"mig57-040","type":"text","x":260,"y":4380,"width":400,"height":300,"color":"6","text":"## [[迁移的家庭风险分担|异地收入共享如何分担风险]]\n\n冲击不完全同向、共享可信且考虑成本时，家庭可能通过异地收入获得保险。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nDifferently exposed earnings can insure a household when sharing is credible and migration and transfer costs are accounted for.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"mig57-041","type":"text","x":980,"y":4380,"width":400,"height":300,"color":"6","text":"## [[循环迁移]]\n\n同一人在地区或国家之间反复迁移；重复性不同于季节性，统计门槛须另定。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nRepeated movement between areas or countries concerns recurrence, not necessarily seasonality. Measurement thresholds require an explicit definition.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"},
		{"id":"mig57-household-bridge","type":"text","x":40,"y":4720,"width":1560,"height":180,"text":"### 机制与形态分开检验\n\n共同承担风险解释收入安排，循环迁移描述重复移动。看到往返本身不能证明风险下降，也不能推出每位家庭成员都受益。\n\n<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\nRisk sharing explains an income arrangement; circular migration describes repeated movement. Recurrence alone establishes neither lower risk nor gains for every household member.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->"}
	],
	"edges":[
		{"id":"mig57-edge-01","fromNode":"mig57-001","fromSide":"right","toNode":"mig57-002","toSide":"left","label":"检验产出损失"},
